<title>JAPAN: Nissho Iwai sets terms on 5 bln yen FRN.</title>
<headline>Nissho Iwai sets terms on 5 bln yen FRN.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>BORROWER - Nissho Iwai Corp</p>
<p>LEAD MGR - Sanwa Securities</p>
<p>FISCAL AGENT - Sanwa Bank</p>
<p> TYPE   FRN	     ISSUE NO   8	  AMT	 5 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON		   ISS PRICE  par	MATURITY 17.June.02</p>
<p> LAST MOODY'S	   PAY DATE 17.June.97 INT PAY 17 June/Dec</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P		 SIGN DATE	     SUB DATE</p>
<p> LAST JCR		 LAST JBRI  A	  LAST NIS   A</p>
<p>NOTE - The coupon on the FRN (floating rate note) will be 0.7 percent above the six-month Euroyen LIBOR (London Interbank Offered Rate), but the upper limit of the coupon will be 1.7 percent for the first year, 2.0 percent for the second year, 2.3 percent for the third year, 3.0 percent for the fourth year, and 3.5 percent for the fifth year.</p>
</text>
